-- title:
--   Adic Galois representation attached to a Hecke character of J₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$, let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $p \ne q$, $q \mid M$, $q^2 \nmid M$ and $5 \le M/q$; let $O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K$, let $i_0 \colon \mathbb{Z}_p \to O$ be a ring homomorphism, and assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Give $J_1(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the Hecke-algebra structure `heckeModuleOneBar M`. Then for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda$ from `rationalHeckeAlgebraOne p (JOne M)` — the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_1(M))$ generated by the image of the Hecke representation — to $K$ such that $\Lambda$ agrees with $i_0$ followed by $O \to K$ on the scalars $\mathbb{Z}_p$, and such that $\Lambda$ annihilates $\sum_d \langle d \rangle$, the sum of the diamond operators over $d < M$ coprime to $M$ with $d \equiv 1 \bmod M/q$, there exists a rank-two adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $O$, that is, a finite free $O$-module $V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from the automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ to $\mathrm{End}_O V$ which is adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ has its pointwise stabiliser acting trivially modulo $\mathfrak{m}_O^n \cdot V$), with the following four properties. (1) For every prime $\ell \nmid Mp$ and $a, d \in O$ with $\Lambda(T_\ell) = a$ and $\Lambda(\langle \ell \rangle) \cdot d = 1$ in $K$, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $\ell$ in its nonunits and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - (da)X + d\ell$. (2) $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of any valuation subring lying over a prime $\ell \nmid Mp$. (3) For every valuation subring $P$ with $q$ in its nonunits, every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup at $P$, every natural number $u \equiv 1 \bmod M/q$ with $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^u$ for all $\zeta$ with $\zeta^q = 1$, and every $d' \in O$ with $\Lambda(\langle u \rangle) \cdot d' = 1$, one has $(\rho(\sigma) - 1)(\rho(\sigma) - d') = 0$ in $\mathrm{End}_O V$. (4) For such $P$, $\sigma$, $u$, $d'$, and in addition any $\tau$ in the decomposition group at $P$ acting on the residue field by $x \mapsto x^q$ and any $t \in O$ with $\Lambda(T_q) = t$, one has $(t\,\rho(\tau) - q)(\rho(\sigma) - d') = 0$.
--
--   This is the construction, from a $K$-valued character of the rational Hecke–diamond algebra acting on the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_1(M)$, of the associated two-dimensional $O$-adic Galois representation, together with its local description: Eichler–Shimura relations at primes away from $Mp$, unramifiedness there, and at the prime $q$ exactly dividing $M$ the ramified-principal-series shape, inertia satisfying a quadratic relation and Frobenius composed with the Hecke operator at $q$ acting as $q$ on the image of $\rho(\sigma) - d'$. It feeds the two statements attaching adic representations to primitive cusp forms that are used in the level-lowering step.
